Replace the Node‑style env access with Vite's `import.meta.env` (or another build‑time injection) and provide a safe fallback. For example:
```tsx
// app/root.tsx
const baseUrl = (
  import.meta.env.VITE_OMNIBRIDGE_PUBLIC_BASE_URL ??
  "https://omnibridge-dev.vercel.app/api/v1"
).replace(/"/g, "\\\"");
```
Then update the Vite config to expose `VITE_OMNIBRIDGE_PUBLIC_BASE_URL`.
Also simplify the script injection:
```tsx
<script
  dangerouslySetInnerHTML={{
    __html: `window.__OMNIBRIDGE_BASE_URL__ = ${JSON.stringify(baseUrl)};`
  }}
/>
```
